    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="13.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ine">Ine</ref> 13.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="13.1" corresp="#wit-e"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="**" target="#Ine_13-1.lnote.oe.star2-2"/><pb n="94" ed="#liebermann"/>Ðeofas we hatað oð VII<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#Ine_13-1.lnote.oe.16"/> men; from VII<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#Ine_13-1.lnote.oe.16"/> hloð oð XXXV<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#Ine_13-1.lnote.oe.17"/>; siððan bið here.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="13.1" corresp="#wit-bu"><pb n="94" ed="#liebermann"/>LVIII. . . . fas we hatað VII men; from VII hloð . . XXXV; siððan bið here.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="13.1" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="94" ed="#liebermann"/>LVIII. Þeofas we hatað oð seofon m<hi rend="italic">en</hi>; from<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_13-1.lnote.oe.1"/> seofon monnum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_13-1.lnote.oe.1"/> hloð oþ XXXV; siððan bið here.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="13.1" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_13-1.lnote.oe.4"/><pb n="95" ed="#liebermann"/>hloðe. Þeofas<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_13-1.lnote.oe.5"/> we hatað oð seofen m<hi rend="italic">en</hi>; fro<hi rend="italic">m<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Ine_13-1.lnote.oe.6"/></hi> seofon hloð oð fif an<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Ine_13-1.lnote.oe.7"/> ðrittig [⁊<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Ine_13-1.lnote.oe.8"/> syððan] here.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="13.1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="95" ed="#liebermann"/>Fures<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="**" target="#Ine_13-1.lnote.oe.star2"/> nominamus usque ad VII<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#Ine_13-1.lnote.oe.20"/> homines; a septem hloþ (id est cohortem uel satellites) usque ad XXXV<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#Ine_13-1.lnote.oe.21"/>; deinceps est<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#Ine_13-1.lnote.oe.22"/> here (id est exercitus).</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="40" ed="#attenborough"/>[(Be) hloðe.] Ðeofas we hatað oð VII men; from VII<ptr type="editorNote" n="8" target="#Ine_13-1.attnote.fn.8"/> hloð oð XXXV; siððan bið here.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="14" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="380" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Ðeofas we hateð oð VII men; from VII hloð oð XXXV; siððen bið here.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="95" ed="#liebermann"/>‘Diebe’ nennen wir [Personen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_13-1.lnote.de.1"/>] bis 7 Mann; von 7<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_13-1.lnote.de.2"/> bis 35: ‘Bande’<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_13-1.lnote.de.3"/>; darüber hinaus ist [es] ein ‘Heer’.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_13-1.lnote.de.4"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">We call [persons] up to 7 men ‘thieves’; from 7 to 35, a ‘band’; beyond that it is an ‘army’.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="41" ed="#attenborough"/>We use the term 'thieves' if the number of men does not exceed seven, 'band of marauders' for a number between seven and thirty-five. Anything beyond this is a 'raid.'</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="401" ed="#whitelock"/>We call up to seven men “thieves”; from seven to thirty-five a “band”; above that it is an “army”.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="381" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>[A group of] up to seven men we call thieves; from seven to thirty-five a band; more is a troop.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:App-AGu_2-2">App AGu 2.2</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="251"><label>cf. (term here 'troop')</label> <ref target="clause:Af_El-to-28">Af El 28</ref> <quote>Cf. Ine §14, where a group in excess of thirty-five men is designated a here ("troop").</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="280"><label>gloss to</label> <ref target="clause:Af_29">Af 29–31.1</ref> <quote>look like glosses to Ine. Some extended Ine's coverage (n. 78: Af 29 – 31:1/Ine 13:1 – 15:1 (gangs))</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="323"><label>cf.</label> <ref target="clause:Af_29">Af 29</ref> <quote>Between seven and thirty-five men, according to Ine §14.</quote></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_13-1.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">95</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">da erster Buchst. klein, wohl</hi> Be <hi rend="italic">davor zu ergänzen</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">since the first letter is small, Be should probably be supplied before it</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_13-1.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">95</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Ð <hi rend="italic">über</hi> þ <hi rend="italic">später</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Ð written above þ later</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_13-1.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">95</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">folgt</hi> seo, <hi rend="italic">aber ausradirt</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">followed by seo, but erased</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_13-1.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">95</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_13-1.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">95</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">⁊ s. <hi rend="italic">im</hi> 16. <hi rend="italic">Jh. eingefügt</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">⁊ s. inserted in the 16th cent.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_13-1.lnote.oe.star2" n="**" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">95</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Fures — redimat uel sic neget (<hi rend="italic">d. i. Ine</hi> 13, 1 — 15) <hi rend="italic">auch App. A Gu.</hi> 2, 2—2,4, <hi rend="italic">doch ohne die</hi> (<hi rend="italic">hier eingeklammerten</hi>) <hi rend="italic">Glossen.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Fures — redimat uel sic neget (i.e. Ine 13, 1 — 15) also App. A Gu. 2, 2—2,4, but without the glosses (here in brackets).</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_13-1.lnote.oe.20" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">95</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">VI <hi rend="italic">R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">VI R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_13-1.lnote.oe.21" n="21" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">95</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">XXV <hi rend="italic">Lond TMHkBr; verb.</hi> XXXV <hi rend="italic">Co Or;</hi> homines <hi rend="italic">fügt zu App. A Gu.</hi> (<hi rend="italic">s. o. S.</hi> 93*)</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">XXV Lond TMHkBr; corrected to XXXV Co Or; homines added by App. A Gu. (see above p. 93*)</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_13-1.lnote.oe.22" n="22" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">95</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_13-1.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">94</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o <hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o altered to a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_13-1.lnote.oe.star2-2" n="**" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">94</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Archetyp zählte</hi> 13,1 <hi rend="italic">mit</hi> 14 [<hi rend="italic">besser</hi>] <hi rend="italic">als</hi> LVIII, <hi rend="italic">laut Bu H B Quadr. Inst. Cnuti.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The archetype numbered 13,1 together with 14 [more correctly] as LVIII, according to Bu H B Quadr. Inst. Cnuti.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_13-1.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">94</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">seofon <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">seofon Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_13-1.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">94</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">fif ⁊ þrittig ⁊ syþþan here <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">fif ⁊ þrittig ⁊ syþþan here Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_13-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">70</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Davor müsste neues Kapitel beginnen. <hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Bande 1. 7. Zu den Zahlen des Kollektivverbrechens <hi rend="italic">vgl.</hi> K. Maurer in <hi rend="italic">Zs. Vereins Volkskunde</hi> 1894, 442</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">A new chapter ought to begin before this. <hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Bande 1. 7. On the numbers in collective crime <hi rend="italic">cf.</hi> K. Maurer in <hi rend="italic">Zs. Vereins Volkskunde</hi> 1894, 442</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_13-1.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">70</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘Männern’ ergänzt unnötig H</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">H unnecessarily adds ‘men’</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_13-1.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">70</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Nicht ‘Beutezug’ und ‘Heereszug’, was zu vorigem ‘Diebe’ nicht passt. <hi rend="italic">Vgl.</hi> Af 29ff.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Not ‘plundering expedition’ and ‘military expedition’, which does not fit the preceding ‘thieves’. <hi rend="italic">Cf.</hi> Af 29ff.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_13-1.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">70</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Heer Z. 4</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Heer l. 4</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_13-1.attnote.fn.8" n="8" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">40</biblScope></bibl><label>vii</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">seofon monnum</hi>. H.</seg></note>
      </div>
